    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41714" root="وجز" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوجَزٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوجِزٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَجْزٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">موجز</span>: [so in the L and TA: it may be either <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوجَزٌ</span>
or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوجِزٌ</span>:] <i>One of the names of</i> [<i>the month of</i>]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَفَر</span>: [app. for one or other of the reasons mentioned voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَفَرٌ</span>:] thought by ISd, to be an
appellation used in the time of the tribe of 'Ád
[who are also said to have called this month
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاجِرٌ</span>]. (L, TA.)

